00:13:57.129 --> 00:14:01.409
That guy looked like a, like someone drew him, you know, he was unbelievable.
那个家伙看起来就像，就像有人把他画出来一样，你知道，简直难以置信。

00:14:01.409 --> 00:14:13.769
The character behind that wall, it really made me laugh because I had, I read the whole book and then watched the episode and I was like, how did an Asha Perlman character get episode 2006 of Howie Nate Your Mother.
墙后面的那个角色真的让我大笑，因为我读完整本书然后看了这一集，我在想，阿沙·普尔曼笔下的角色怎么会跑到《老爸老妈浪漫史》第2006集里去的。

00:14:13.769 --> 00:14:15.490
See, it changes over time.
你看，它是随时间变化的。

00:14:15.490 --> 00:14:20.529
Like we're saying in the opening, we change this as you change full circle.
就像我们在开场所说的那样，随着你的改变，我们也在改变，一切又回到了起点。

00:14:20.529 --> 00:14:31.409
But no, I did want to talk about another wonderful constructed shot by our wonderful director and camera crew, which is that reveal, right?
不过说真的，我确实想谈谈由我们出色的导演和摄影团队精心设计的另一个精彩镜头，也就是那个特写揭秘，对吧？

00:14:31.409 --> 00:14:36.090
I was talking to you guys before we recorded about that reveal that is a Cone Brother shout out.
我们在录制前聊天时，我跟你们提过那个致敬科恩兄弟的揭秘镜头。

00:14:36.090 --> 00:14:37.409
Can I talk about that for a second?
我能聊这个一会儿吗？

00:14:37.409 --> 00:14:38.730
Please.
请便。

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:44.450
I've been rearing to get to this and no one will care or know what I'm talking about, but I'm just gonna do it anyway because it makes me happy.
我一直急着想聊这个，虽然可能没人关心或者听不懂我在说什么，但我还是要讲，因为这让我很开心。

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:48.289
In the movie, Miller's Crossing, which is one of my favorite films, and Carter II.
在电影《米勒的十字路口》里，那是我最喜欢的电影之一，还有《巴顿·芬克》。

00:14:48.289 --> 00:15:11.649
There's this moment where Tom Regan, is played by Gabriel Byrne, enters his own apartment, comes down, the phone's ringing, it's late at night, he sits down, answers the phone, and you're just tight on Gabriel Byrne, and he has an entire phone call, hangs up the phone, and he's the whole time he's looking kind of past camera, you're right in his face, And then he hangs up a phone and he goes, hello, Bernie.
有这样一个场景：由加布里埃尔·伯恩饰演的汤姆·里根走进自己的公寓，走进来，电话在响，当时已经是深夜，他坐下，接起电话，镜头一直紧紧对准加布里埃尔·伯恩，他打了一整通电话，挂断电话，整个过程他都把目光投向镜头之外，你就直面着他的脸，然后他挂了电话说，你好，伯尼。

00:15:11.649 --> 00:15:19.850
And you reveal that that entire time Bernie Burnbound, John Tataro, had broken into his apartment and was sitting there.
接着镜头一转，你才发现原来伯尼·伯恩鲍姆（约翰·特托罗饰）不知什么时候潜入了他的公寓，一直在那里坐着。

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:25.289
And there's this incredibly ominous reveal because it's definitely trouble that this guy is sitting there.
这个出场揭秘极其不祥，因为这家伙坐在那儿绝对意味着麻烦。

00:15:25.289 --> 00:15:29.450
And you're so long just on Tom Regan, Gabriel Byrne.
而且镜头长时间只对着汤姆·里根，也就是加布里埃尔·伯恩。

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:33.529
And then all of a sudden it's this reveal after a long phone called that Bernie's there.
然后在经历了一场漫长的电话之后，突然揭晓伯尼其实一直都在。

00:15:33.529 --> 00:15:36.690
Well, that's exactly what we did with Barney.
这正是我们对巴尼的处理方式。

00:15:36.690 --> 00:15:38.289
Barney walks in, he's on his earpiece.
巴尼走进来，戴着耳机。

00:15:38.289 --> 00:15:44.409
He's having this long phone call, having this like angry, like threatening call that turns out to be with his own mother.
他在打一通漫长的电话，语气生气且充满威胁，结果发现电话是打给他亲妈的。

00:15:44.409 --> 00:15:52.370
And then after a really long cross, only on him, you reveal and it's all in one shot, which is not true in the bonus crossing.
接着在长时间只有他的过肩镜头之后，镜头突然拉开——这在《米勒的十字路口》里是没有的。

00:15:52.370 --> 00:15:56.610
But it's all in shot that you sort of wide now enough to see Lily's just been sitting there the whole time.
但这是一个一气呵成的镜头，镜头拉得足够宽，让你看到莉莉其实一直都在那儿坐着。

00:15:56.610 --> 00:15:57.610
Hello, Lily.
你好，莉莉。

00:15:57.610 --> 00:16:06.769
See, you guys, you guys had the audacity and the technical know how to pull off a wonder that the Coen brothers couldn't possibly have figured out.
看吧，你们这群人居然有这种厚脸皮和技术水平，能拍出一个科恩兄弟绝对想不出来的奇观。

00:16:06.769 --> 00:16:08.809
The con runners don't know how to move a camera.
那些联合主创根本不知道怎么移动摄像机。

00:16:08.809 --> 00:16:09.850
That's what I'm saying.
我是这个意思。

00:16:09.850 --> 00:16:14.450
Yeah, you know, it's also a great thing when you're an artist.
对，你知道的，当你成为一名艺术家时，这也是件很棒的事。

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:29.009
You watch movies and you read books and we've talked so much about all the crazy kind of influences and even on subtle levels, you know, when you're doing things, you might not even realize you're paying homage to something or ripping it off outright.
你看电影，读书，我们讨论过那么多疯狂的影响，甚至在潜移默化的层面上，当你创作时，你可能甚至没有意识到自己在向什么东西致敬，或者根本就是赤裸裸地抄袭。

00:16:29.009 --> 00:16:31.690
But it's so much fun to have a vocabulary.
但拥有这样一套语汇真的很有趣。

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:32.529
Yeah.
对。

00:16:32.529 --> 00:16:40.049
To have a vocabulary to talk about these things speaking shorthand with, you know, a DP or so, you know, who might have the same references.
拥有共同的语汇来谈论这些事情，能和那些有着相同观影参考的摄影指导（DP）或其他人进行简短高效的交流。

00:16:40.049 --> 00:16:40.549
