00:56:49.239 --> 00:56:51.485
Me and the champ are going over here.
我和冠军要去那边。

00:56:51.485 --> 00:56:59.980
And then I'm like, yeah, so me and the champ are going to get out of here and he goes, method, he was the baby was method into my chest mic.
然后我说，好，所以我和冠军要离开这儿了，结果他发出了声音，这小家伙太懂得利用我胸前的麦克风了。

00:56:59.980 --> 00:57:01.072
It's just as crap.
直接拉了。

00:57:01.072 --> 00:57:03.500
Somewhere that footage exists somewhere.
那个素材肯定还在某个地方。

00:57:03.500 --> 00:57:06.313
Well, howling behind the monitors.
好吧，大家在监视器后面笑得前仰后合。

00:57:06.313 --> 00:57:11.111
And like, my next line is like, whoa, do you want to come?
然后我的下一句台词是，哇，你想来吗？

00:57:11.111 --> 00:57:15.827
Do you want to come clean and admit that wasn't the baby?
你想来坦白承认那其实不是婴儿拉的吗？

00:57:15.827 --> 00:57:17.400
It's been 20 years.
已经过去20年了。

00:57:17.400 --> 00:57:18.448
You can tell us.
你可以告诉我们。

00:57:18.448 --> 00:57:19.497
You can tell us.
你可以告诉我们。

00:57:19.497 --> 00:57:20.480
Sorry, America.
对不起，美国。

00:57:20.480 --> 00:57:22.183
You never get to see that.
你们永远看不到了。

00:57:22.183 --> 00:57:26.640
It was funny and it didn't go and it was one of those hard breakers.
它很有趣，但没能被砍掉，而且这是一个让人心碎的时刻。

00:57:26.639 --> 00:57:29.440
But thank God, thank God you were Brad.
但谢天谢地，谢天谢地你是布拉德。

00:57:29.440 --> 00:57:39.719
Thank God you were so fucking funny that we kept bringing you back and maybe we will bring you back on here if you're around to talk about one of these crazy, huge EPs that you're in because you were so fucking great.
谢天谢地你他妈的太有趣了，以至于我们一直把你请回来，也许以后你如果方便的话，我们还会请你来聊聊你参演的那些疯狂的大热剧集，因为你他妈的太棒了。

00:57:39.719 --> 00:57:43.760
We just here for years and years and years of how much people love you on the show.
我们只是在这里度过了多年又多年，听到人们有多么喜欢你在剧中的表现。

00:57:43.760 --> 00:57:44.800
That's why we kept bringing you back.
这就是为什么我们一直把你请回来。

00:57:44.800 --> 00:57:45.840
That's why we did that pilot.
这也是为什么我们拍了那部试播集。

00:57:45.840 --> 00:57:49.800
I wish we could have done even more, but man, thank you for being on this TV show.
我希望我们能拍更多，但老兄，谢谢你来出演这部电视剧。

00:57:49.800 --> 00:57:54.239
You were so funny and it's just like, we're honored that you're part of this universe, man.
你太搞笑了，我们真的很荣幸你能成为这个宇宙的一部分，老兄。

00:57:54.239 --> 00:57:57.039
Joe Mangadallo, thank you for being with us, buddy.
乔·曼根尼罗（Joe Manganiello），谢谢你和我们在一起，伙计。

00:57:57.039 --> 00:57:57.840
Yeah, man.
好兄弟。

00:57:57.840 --> 00:57:58.719
Great to see you.
很高兴见到你。

00:57:58.719 --> 00:58:05.679
Thanks for dropping by.
谢谢你抽空过来。

00:58:05.679 --> 00:58:10.800
One of our favorite parts of doing this podcast is hearing from the fans and hearing from you guys.
做这个播客最让我们喜欢的部分之一，就是倾听粉丝的心声，听听你们的反馈。

00:58:10.800 --> 00:58:13.239
You can reach out to us at how we made your mother.com.
你可以通过 how we made your mother.com 联系我们。

00:58:13.239 --> 00:58:15.039
Go to contact and write us a message.
点击“联系我们”并给我们留言。

00:58:15.039 --> 00:58:16.719
You can submit audio messages.
你可以提交语音留言。

00:58:16.719 --> 00:58:19.519
And you might hear it or hear us read it on the show.
你可能会在节目中听到它，或者听到我们朗读它。

00:58:19.519 --> 00:58:21.840
And it's always one of our favorite parts.
这总是我们最喜欢的环节之一。

00:58:21.840 --> 00:58:24.880
And here's one, a case in point.
这就是一个很好的例子。

00:58:24.880 --> 00:58:32.351
And the funny thing is, this episode this week, the episode we're talking about World's Greatest Couple, written by Brenda Shea, and this is a Brenda, another Brenda.
有趣的是，本周的这一集，也就是我们正在讨论的《世界上最棒的情侣》（World's Greatest Couple），由布伦达·谢（Brenda Shea）编剧，这也是一个叫布伦达的人。

00:58:32.351 --> 00:58:36.042
I hope it's not Brenda Shea writing to the show, but that would seem like a cheat.
我希望写信给节目的不是布伦达·谢本人，但这听起来有点像作弊。

00:58:36.042 --> 00:58:38.833
We'd like to formally dedicate this episode to all the Brenda.
我们要把这一集正式献给所有的布伦达。

00:58:38.833 --> 00:58:39.823
Everyone named Brenda.
所有叫布伦达的人。

00:58:39.823 --> 00:58:42.794
It's just Brenda talking about how much she liked her own episode.
这其实只是布伦达在说她有多喜欢她自己写的这一集。

00:58:42.794 --> 00:58:45.719
Now, it's Brenda from New Jersey, and here's what she has to say.
不，这是来自新泽西的布伦达，以下是她想说的话。

00:58:46.440 --> 00:58:47.101
Hi, everyone.
大家好。

00:58:47.101 --> 00:58:52.597
I cannot truly find the words to describe how much the show means to me and how deeply I've come to love it.
我真的找不到言语来形容这部剧对我意味着什么，以及我是多么深深地爱着它。

00:58:52.597 --> 00:58:56.464
I am currently 29 years old and have watched this show since I was about 17.
我今年29岁，从大约17岁起就开始看这部剧了。

00:58:56.464 --> 00:59:03.690
I've re-watched the entire series more times than I could count and leaned on it as a source of comfort to all stages of my adult life so far.
整部剧我重刷了无数次，在我目前成年生活的各个阶段，它都是我寻求慰藉的源泉。

00:59:03.690 --> 00:59:07.711
I learn new lessons and connect with new themes in the show every time I watch.
每次看这部剧，我都能学到新的教训，并与新的主题产生共鸣。

00:59:07.711 --> 00:59:19.059
My long-term relationship of six years has hit a crossroads and I've been having strong feelings for some time now that I need to separate and go down my own path in order to chase my dreams and feel fulfilled with my life.
我这段维持了六年的长期恋爱关系遇到了十字路口，一段时间以来，我强烈地感觉到我需要分开，走我自己的路，去追逐我的梦想，让我的生活感到充实。

00:59:19.059 --> 00:59:25.216
I love my partner very much and do want to marry him one day, and that is the goal we have been working towards recently.
我非常爱我的伴侣，有一天确实想和他结婚，这也是我们最近一直在努力的目标。

00:59:25.216 --> 00:59:32.697
But I am at a point right now where I feel stuck and unsure if I can move forward with marriage without pursuing some other life experiences first.
但我现在处于这样一个阶段：我感到困惑，如果不先追求其他的人生经历，我不确定自己是否能迈入婚姻的殿堂。

00:59:32.697 --> 00:59:41.449
I really relate to Lilly in these last few episodes needing to put herself first and feeling anxious about tying the knot without getting to travel and pursue her passions.
我对莉莉在最后这几集里的经历深有同感，她需要把自我放在首位，并且在没有去旅行和追求自己的热情之前，对步入婚姻感到焦虑。

00:59:41.449 --> 00:59:49.337
I wanted to thank you for depicting this struggle in the show and showing us that sometimes you have to make mistakes to know for sure that it's a mistake.
我想感谢你们在剧中描绘了这种挣扎，并向我们展示了有时你必须犯错，才能确切知道这是一个错误。

00:59:49.337 --> 01:00:04.960
It has given me so much comfort rewatching these episodes because even though these are fictional stories it helps to be reminded that even the strongest couples like Marshall and Lily go through struggles and have challenges to overcome and that's okay because what is meant to be will still be in the end.
重温这些剧集给了我极大的安慰，因为尽管这些都是虚构的故事，但它能提醒我们，即便是像马歇尔和莉莉这样最坚固的情侣，也会经历挣扎和需要克服的挑战，这没关系，因为命中注定的事情到头来依然会是注定的。

01:00:05.519 --> 01:00:06.911
That's very wise.
这非常明智。

01:00:06.911 --> 01:00:09.039
Those are very wise words.
这些是非常睿智的话语。

01:00:09.039 --> 01:00:24.719
You know what occurred to me as I was listening to that Craig is you know when you have your first heartbreak or your first career disappointment or like the first of anything is the most devastating, the most calamitous, because you have no evidence that you're going to survive it.
克雷格，当我听到这里时我突然想到，你知道的，当你经历第一次心碎，或者第一次职业上的失望，或者任何事情的“第一次”时，往往是最具毁灭性、最凄惨的，因为你没有任何证据证明自己能挺过去。

01:00:24.719 --> 01:00:25.302
Yes, yes.
是的，是的。

01:00:25.302 --> 01:00:30.800
And then you survive it, and then it happens again, and you go, okay, this is no fun.
然后你挺过来了，接着它又发生了，你会想，好吧，这真的一点也不好玩。

01:00:30.800 --> 01:00:36.046
I still dislike this, but I do have evidence that it is survivable.
我依然讨厌这样，但我确实有了能挺过去的证据。

01:00:36.046 --> 01:00:49.280
And I think in the absence of either an older sibling or an older friend telling you, you know, putting a hand on your on your shoulder saying like, this happened to me.
我想，如果没有年长的兄弟姐妹或年长的朋友告诉你，把手放在你的肩膀上对你说，这种事我也经历过。

01:00:49.280 --> 01:00:52.639
And there's like, yeah, this show can be that for people.
然后就会觉得，是的，这部剧就能为人们扮演这样的角色。

01:00:52.639 --> 01:00:57.199
You can see that, okay, oh, Marshall Lilly broke up and she went off to pursue her, whatever.
你可以看到，好吧，哦，Marshall 和 Lily 分手了，然后她去追求她自己的，随便什么吧。

01:00:57.199 --> 01:01:02.079
And, but they still got back like, or, you know, Ted got heartbroken, but the heart is resilient.
而且，但他们还是复合了，或者，你知道的，Ted 曾心碎过，但心是很有韧性的。

01:01:02.079 --> 01:01:04.880
And like, like, it can work, things can work out.
就像，就像，这是行得通的，事情会有好结果的。

01:01:04.880 --> 01:01:15.920
I think the show can be like a whisper of, it is a whisper of a future self to occurrence self, but it can provide that for the viewers.
我觉得这部剧就像是一种低语，它是把未来的自己对当下的自己的一种低语，但它能为观众提供这种感受。

01:01:15.920 --> 01:01:21.000
Yeah, not only that it's survivable, but that you can be stronger from it, right?
对，不仅说明这并不是绝路，还说明经历之后你会变得更坚强，对吧？

01:01:21.000 --> 01:01:27.719
And like Marshall and Lily get back together, sorry, spoilers, and to come out at the other end stronger.
就像 Marshall 和 Lily 复合了——抱歉，剧透了——然后在另一头变得更强。

01:01:27.719 --> 01:01:35.880
And, you know, some of Marshall and Lily is based on my wife and I, my wife and I did in our twenties to take, we broke up for a little while and we got back together and got married.
而且，你知道的，Marshall 和 Lily 的部分故事是以我和我太太为原型的，我和我太太在二十多岁时，我们分手了一段时间，然后复合并结婚了。

01:01:35.880 --> 01:01:39.960
And it was very much the Marshall and Lily arc and it was really hard.
这非常符合 Marshall 和 Lily 的故事弧光，而且真的很难。

01:01:39.960 --> 01:01:45.320
And, but maybe it was necessary and it went, the story did continue past that.
但是，也许这是必须经历的，而且故事确实在那之后继续了。

01:01:45.320 --> 01:01:52.280
And even if it hadn't, and even if it doesn't for Brenda and that relationship or whatever, it's survivable.
即便没有，即使对 Brenda 和那段感情或别的什么来说没有，这也是能挺过去的。

01:01:52.280 --> 01:01:54.360
It's survivable, and you will come out the other side.
这是能挺过去的，而且你会安然度过。

01:01:54.360 --> 01:01:55.920
I think that's a great way to look at it.
我觉得这是一种很好的看待方式。

01:01:55.920 --> 01:01:59.820
It was a strange moment for me when Rebecca moved in with me.
对我来说，丽贝卡搬来和我一起住的时候是个很奇妙的时刻。

01:01:59.820 --> 01:02:02.000
Are we talking about this finally?
我们终于要聊这个了吗？

01:02:02.000 --> 01:02:03.320
Because I've been waiting to get into this.
因为我等这个话题好久了。

01:02:03.320 --> 01:02:05.400
And help me with my one nice dance.
帮我跳那段美好的舞蹈。

01:02:05.400 --> 01:02:09.800
Yeah, so you are the Barney and our friend group.
对，所以你是我们朋友圈里的 Barney。

01:02:09.800 --> 01:02:10.639
That's the weird thing.
这就是奇怪的地方。

01:02:10.639 --> 01:02:14.239
It's very confusing, but you played Ted on the show.
这太让人混乱了，但你在剧里演的是 Ted。

01:02:14.239 --> 01:02:14.856
phenomenal.
太绝了。

01:02:14.856 --> 01:02:16.483
Well that was a great letter.
好吧，那真是一封很棒的信。

01:02:16.483 --> 01:02:21.811
I'm so glad that people engage with the show at these moments that are like crossroads moments.
我很高兴人们在这些人生十字路口的时刻能与这部剧产生共鸣。

01:02:21.811 --> 01:02:23.269
I think that was her word.
我想那是她用的词。

01:02:23.269 --> 01:02:30.448
Crossroads moments of life and I like that the perspective of the show can let people know there's another there's another side.
人生的十字路口，我喜欢这部剧的视角能让人们知道，还有另一条路，还有另一面。

01:02:30.448 --> 01:02:35.160
You will cross that raging river and you will get somewhere else and you'll be okay.
你会渡过那条汹涌的河流，你会到达别的地方，你会好起来的。

01:02:35.159 --> 01:02:38.870
Yeah big thanks to Joe Manganela for joining us today.
是的，非常感谢乔·曼根尼罗今天加入我们。

01:02:38.870 --> 01:02:46.840
It was so much fun and Craig great to be with you today and Alec and our gang over here and we'll see you next time.
这真的太有趣了，Craig，很高兴今天能和你在一起，还有 Alec 以及我们这里的伙伴们，我们下次见。

01:02:46.840 --> 01:02:49.320
Thanks for watching along with us.
感谢大家一路陪伴收看。

